WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.580
- Why is it important
to uplift other women

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.100
in all areas of life?

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.673
Like I feel like for me personally,

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.070
I feel like it's the change won't happen

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.890
unless we are daily supporting each other,

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.510
and not in competition all
the time with each other,

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.470
like obviously you're on the court,

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.303
you're in competition with people,

00:00:17.303 --> 00:00:19.030
obviously I'm up against
awards or whatever,

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.690
but at the end of the day,
there's room for everyone,

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.010
and I feel like it's really important

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.300
for women to do that for women,

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.770
more so than men sticking up for us,

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:28.670
because I think that sets the example.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:29.550
Do you agree?

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.620
- Yes. That's literally
what I say all the time.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.740
Like literally I say,
there's room for all of us.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.640
This is such a big planet,
there's room for so many of us

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.000
to have our own successful companies,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.270
have our own TV shows,

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:46.000
like, to win grand slams,
there's four a year,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.450
like there's so many opportunities,

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:53.850
and I just like, I don't
understand why it has to be,

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.380
it's a competition, and believe me,

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.130
when I'm out there, I
give a zillion percent.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.420
But at the end of the
day, if someone else wins

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.010
or if someone has a successful company,

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:06.040
I'm genuinely happy for
them because first of all,

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.000
that affects my energy if I'm
not, and it affects who I am,

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.570
and it makes me even to be around me,

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:15.200
I just lose this glow,
and I don't want that.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.690
And second of all, jealousy
is rottenness to the bone,

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.510
and I never want to do that.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.210
And I feel like women should...

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.400
The success, I say the
success of one woman

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.404
should be the inspiration
to another, and I love that.

00:01:29.404 --> 00:01:32.620
I love saying that because it's inspiring.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.450
Like, oh my gosh sister you've made it.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.780
This is great. I can do it too.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.500
And that's what I think a lot of men do.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.250
And I really, really, truly believe

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.060
a lot of women are leaning
into this so much more.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.590
I can see it now, like even
when I'm in my job in tennis,

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:49.690
so many women are so
happy for the next person

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.070
and it's just such a
different environment,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.400
and it's happening,

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.140
and that's what's the most exciting thing.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.710
So I'm really excited to see that,

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.170
us being happy for each other.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:00.490
Cause that's what it's about.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:01.410
- Yeah. I also think it's-

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:02.243
- Life's too short

00:02:02.243 --> 00:02:06.080
- Yeah, especially as mothers
of daughters and sons,

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.920
like it's really cool for us to like,

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.790
I find that that's my
biggest responsibility,

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:12.170
is showing her how to treat
other women in my business,

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:14.900
or people that I work with, or...

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.550
We're the best, we're going
to be the best example

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:18.680
because they're going
to follow our actions

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:19.960
not our words necessarily.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.220
So I think that's the
cool thing too as a mom,

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.570
you get to show how to show
respect to other women,

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:27.740
instead of be envious,
instead of go for jealousy,

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.090
instead of all of that, so.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.490
I don't know. Do you feel that as a mama?

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:31.700
I feel like that's my biggest thing.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.050
I'm like, just don't fail as a mom.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.660
I can fail as a singer, I
can fail as everything else,

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.070
but I don't want to fail as a mom.

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.007
That's my biggest thing.

00:02:38.007 --> 00:02:41.770
- Oh that's so sweet. Yeah. No, I agree.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:44.710
Cause you are lead by
example, not by words,

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.010
and actually lead by both,

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:48.053
but definitely by example as well.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:52.040
And like, you don't want negative
energy going to your kid,

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.840
you know, that's not cool.

